WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.268 --> 00:00:04.435
♫ Singing this song blesses me. ♫

00:00:07.218 --> 00:00:09.586
- [Voiceover] Death being
like a song, takes place

00:00:09.586 --> 00:00:11.251
over time.

00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:14.995
There's a beginning to
it, there's a culmination,

00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:16.322
and then there's an ending.

00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:20.313
I think it has the possibility
of enhancing our lives

00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:23.980
rather than taking
something away from them.

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:26.826
My name is Kate Munger, I'm the founder of

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.433
The Threshold Choir.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:31.066
We sing at the bedsides
of people who are dying.

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:34.149
(singing in harmony)

00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:39.176
I started the first
choir in March of 2000.

00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:42.010
Six months later, two
more choirs, and today

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:44.337
there are 150 choirs around the world.

00:00:44.337 --> 00:00:48.504
♫ May you be at peace. ♫

00:00:51.137 --> 00:00:54.617
In 1990, I spent an
afternoon taking care of

00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:57.577
a friend of mine who
was dying of HIV/AIDS.

00:00:57.577 --> 00:01:01.275
He was comatose and
agitated, and I didn't know

00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:02.562
what to do.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.062
So I started instinctively singing to him.

00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:10.227
He started to calm and I started to calm.

00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:13.449
I knew I'd discovered something ancient,

00:01:13.449 --> 00:01:16.116
and that I wanted to bring back.

00:01:18.497 --> 00:01:21.161
The songs that we bring to
bedsides are mostly songs

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:22.697
that we've written.

00:01:22.697 --> 00:01:26.274
They're short, they're
sung very, very softly,

00:01:26.274 --> 00:01:31.256
and the lyrics offer
comfort, they offer serenity,

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:33.839
they offer simplicity and ease.

00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:43.193
We will knock on the door
and try to slip into the room

00:01:43.193 --> 00:01:47.360
where the person is dying,
as gently as a butterfly.

00:01:48.596 --> 00:01:50.729
We've come to sing for you.

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:54.896
♫ May you be free from suffering. ♫

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:02.393
We often see a calming
of the breath, sometimes

00:02:02.393 --> 00:02:06.170
we'll see a toe tapping
or a finger moving,

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:10.337
a smile, and then when we're
done, slip out just as quietly.

00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:15.170
Often we'll leave singing.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:19.337
♫ You are not alone, I am here now. ♫

00:02:26.906 --> 00:02:28.753
Many of the people we've sung for say that

00:02:28.753 --> 00:02:32.130
their pain is gone,
their pain is lessened,

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.816
that is a miracle to me.

00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:37.899
(gentle piano music)

